WEBVTT

00:00.410 --> 00:02.025
Before we look at numbers,

00:02.025 --> 00:03.330
let's quickly review.

00:03.770 --> 00:06.500
In the last video, we looked at tense.

00:07.000 --> 00:08.599
If the line is solid,

00:08.599 --> 00:10.884
the data has already happened.

00:10.884 --> 00:13.930
So we use the past simple: cycling rose.

00:14.780 --> 00:16.467
If the line is dashed,

00:16.467 --> 00:18.537
it's probably a projection.

00:18.537 --> 00:20.377
So we use a future form.

00:20.377 --> 00:23.213
For example, it is expected to reach,

00:23.213 --> 00:25.360
or it is predicted to reach,

00:25.360 --> 00:27.430
or it is forecast to reach.

00:27.930 --> 00:30.099
And before that, you learned to choose a

00:30.099 --> 00:31.400
precise verb and adverb,

00:31.700 --> 00:34.500
like rose sharply or fell gradually.

00:35.060 --> 00:36.911
Now, let's add the numbers.

00:36.911 --> 00:38.899
When I was an IELTS examiner,

00:38.899 --> 00:41.709
small words like "by" and "to" were often

00:41.709 --> 00:44.040
what made a sentence about numbers

00:44.410 --> 00:46.310
accurate or inaccurate.

00:46.740 --> 00:47.970
So let's get them right.

00:48.500 --> 00:50.250
Look at cycling on this graph.

00:50.680 --> 00:53.480
In 2000, it was 12%.

00:54.420 --> 00:57.410
In 2020, it was 34%.

00:57.980 --> 01:00.294
There are three different things I could

01:00.294 --> 01:01.220
tell the reader.

01:01.750 --> 01:05.320
If I want the size of the change, I use "by".

01:05.690 --> 01:09.380
Cycling rose by 22 percentage points.

01:09.380 --> 01:12.970
If I want the end point, I use "to".

01:13.500 --> 01:18.760
Car use fell to 37% in 2020.

01:19.260 --> 01:22.258
If I want both the start and the end,

01:22.258 --> 01:24.040
I use "from" and "to".

01:24.470 --> 01:28.840
Cycling rose from 12% to 34%.

01:29.400 --> 01:31.937
If there's no change and I just want the

01:31.937 --> 01:34.410
level at one point in time, I use "at".

01:34.740 --> 01:39.010
Cycling stood at 12% in 2000.

01:39.540 --> 01:43.010
And if I use a noun instead of a verb, I need "of".

01:43.420 --> 01:46.790
There was a rise of 22 percentage points.

01:47.290 --> 01:50.690
So remember, a verb takes "by" and a noun takes "of".

01:51.220 --> 01:55.850
Rose by 22 points. A rise of 22 points.

01:56.340 --> 01:59.270
One mistake I see a lot is "increased of".

01:59.580 --> 02:01.149
"Increased" is a verb,

02:01.149 --> 02:02.790
so it's "increased by".

02:03.320 --> 02:05.461
And a quick note. When a percentage

02:05.461 --> 02:07.479
changes, we measure the change in

02:07.479 --> 02:08.580
percentage points.

02:08.920 --> 02:12.420
12% to 34% is 22

02:12.700 --> 02:13.830
percentage points.

02:14.360 --> 02:16.904
Now, try the activity next to the video

02:16.904 --> 02:20.230
and choose the right preposition for each sentence.
